---
id: exhaustive-deps
title: Exhaustive dependencies for query keys
---
NIFT_TANSTACK_DOCUMENT_V1
{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Query keys should be seen like a dependency array to your query function: Every variable that is used inside the queryFn should be added to the query key.\nThis makes sure that queries are cached independently and that queries are refetched automatically when the variables changes."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"rule-details","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Rule Details"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Examples of "},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"incorrect"}]},{"type":"text","value":" code for this rule:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"/* eslint \"@tanstack/query/exhaustive-deps\": \"error\" */\n\nuseQuery({\n    queryKey: [\"todo\"],\n    queryFn: () => api.getTodo(todoId)\n})\n\nconst todoQueries = {\n    detail: (id) => ({ queryKey: [\"todo\"], queryFn: () => api.getTodo(id) })\n}","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Examples of "},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"correct"}]},{"type":"text","value":" code for this rule:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"useQuery({\n    queryKey: [\"todo\", todoId],\n    queryFn: () => api.getTodo(todoId)\n})\n\nconst todoQueries = {\n    detail: (id) => ({ queryKey: [\"todo\", id], queryFn: () => api.getTodo(id) })\n}","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"when-not-to-use-it","children":[{"type":"text","value":"When Not To Use It"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"If you don't care about the rules of the query keys, then you will not need this rule."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"attributes","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Attributes"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"✅ Recommended"}]}],"checked":true},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"🔧 Fixable"}]}],"checked":true}]}],"headings":[{"id":"rule-details","text":"Rule Details","level":2},{"id":"when-not-to-use-it","text":"When Not To Use It","level":2},{"id":"attributes","text":"Attributes","level":2}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\nQuery keys should be seen like a dependency array to your query function: Every variable that is used inside the queryFn should be added to the query key.\nThis makes sure that queries are cached independently and that queries are refetched automatically when the variables changes.\n\n## Rule Details\n\nExamples of **incorrect** code for this rule:\n\n```tsx\n/* eslint \"@tanstack/query/exhaustive-deps\": \"error\" */\n\nuseQuery({\n    queryKey: [\"todo\"],\n    queryFn: () => api.getTodo(todoId)\n})\n\nconst todoQueries = {\n    detail: (id) => ({ queryKey: [\"todo\"], queryFn: () => api.getTodo(id) })\n}\n```\n\n\nExamples of **correct** code for this rule:\n\n```tsx\nuseQuery({\n    queryKey: [\"todo\", todoId],\n    queryFn: () => api.getTodo(todoId)\n})\n\nconst todoQueries = {\n    detail: (id) => ({ queryKey: [\"todo\", id], queryFn: () => api.getTodo(id) })\n}\n```\n\n## When Not To Use It\n\nIf you don't care about the rules of the query keys, then you will not need this rule.\n\n## Attributes\n\n- [x] ✅ Recommended\n- [x] 🔧 Fixable\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\nid: exhaustive-deps\ntitle: Exhaustive dependencies for query keys\n---\n\nQuery keys should be seen like a dependency array to your query function: Every variable that is used inside the queryFn should be added to the query key.\nThis makes sure that queries are cached independently and that queries are refetched automatically when the variables changes.\n\n## Rule Details\n\nExamples of **incorrect** code for this rule:\n\n```tsx\n/* eslint \"@tanstack/query/exhaustive-deps\": \"error\" */\n\nuseQuery({\n    queryKey: [\"todo\"],\n    queryFn: () => api.getTodo(todoId)\n})\n\nconst todoQueries = {\n    detail: (id) => ({ queryKey: [\"todo\"], queryFn: () => api.getTodo(id) })\n}\n```\n\n\nExamples of **correct** code for this rule:\n\n```tsx\nuseQuery({\n    queryKey: [\"todo\", todoId],\n    queryFn: () => api.getTodo(todoId)\n})\n\nconst todoQueries = {\n    detail: (id) => ({ queryKey: [\"todo\", id], queryFn: () => api.getTodo(id) })\n}\n```\n\n## When Not To Use It\n\nIf you don't care about the rules of the query keys, then you will not need this rule.\n\n## Attributes\n\n- [x] ✅ Recommended\n- [x] 🔧 Fixable\n"}
